  "courseSlug": "nodejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "NodeJS - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342159",
      "title": "Testing the API",
      "lectureOrder": 510,
      "videoOrder": 452,
      "sourceHash": "986cc84e7725ab40e183e98f0337e3019013310e67dd0719b0a6a12209c945ad",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.68,
          "end": 4.09,
          "en": "To test this entire API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.09,
          "end": 6.51,
          "en": "we first of all need to compile it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.51,
          "end": 8.66,
          "en": "And we can just run TSC for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.66,
          "end": 10.01,
          "en": "since this will compile all the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.01,
          "end": 11.763,
          "en": "TypeScript files in this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.17,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "So you see that this completes without errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 16.86,
          "en": "One important note,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.86,
          "end": 18.62,
          "en": "is that in the models folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.62,
          "end": 22.03,
          "en": "you'll see the todo JS file is pretty empty here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.03,
          "end": 23.52,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.52,
          "end": 26.74,
          "en": "interfaces are a pure TypeScript feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.74,
          "end": 29.24,
          "en": "Which helps TypeScript during compilation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.24,
          "end": 31.8,
          "en": "but which generate no actual code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.8,
          "end": 34.61,
          "en": "Because this feature doesn't create anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.61,
          "end": 37.27,
          "en": "that would exist in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.27,
          "end": 39.49,
          "en": "Therefore, we essentially have an empty file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.49,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "without anything in it in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 43.63,
          "en": "if you take a closer look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 43.63,
          "end": 44.94,
          "en": "But our code still works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 44.94,
          "end": 47.08,
          "en": "because that todo interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 47.08,
          "end": 49.94,
          "en": "is only used as a type definition in the other files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 49.94,
          "end": 51.71,
          "en": "Like here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 51.71,
          "end": 52.81,
          "en": "And that's a feature which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 52.81,
          "end": 54.73,
          "en": "doesn't exist in JavaScript anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 54.73,
          "end": 55.64,
          "en": "that's what I mean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 55.64,
          "end": 58.44,
          "en": "it only matters during compilation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 58.44,
          "end": 60.73,
          "en": "We disregard all those JavaScript files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 60.73,
          "end": 63.42,
          "en": "and we can now just run them as we're used to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 63.42,
          "end": 66.57,
          "en": "So here I can just run Node app JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 69.5,
          "en": "and this will spin up our Node Web Server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 69.5,
          "end": 73.2,
          "en": "And we can now test our REST API with Postman,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 73.2,
          "end": 75.403,
          "en": "as we did it before in this course as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 76.61,
          "end": 78.83,
          "en": "Which in case you haven't seen it before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 78.83,
          "end": 80.93,
          "en": "you can download from Postman.com.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 80.93,
          "end": 84.393,
          "en": "It's a tool that can help you with testing REST API's.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 85.6,
          "end": 86.51,
          "en": "And with that opened,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 86.51,
          "end": 89.28999999999999,
          "en": "we can send requests to our running web server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 89.28999999999999,
          "end": 91.73,
          "en": "Which I started with Node app JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 91.73,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "and that's important Node app JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 96.42,
          "en": "not app TS, but app JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 99.16,
          "en": "We can only execute JavaScript code with Node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 99.16,
          "end": 101.97999999999999,
          "en": "Node is not capable of running TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 101.97999999999999,
          "end": 105.4,
          "en": "It's only capable of running JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 105.4,
          "end": 107.74000000000001,
          "en": "Therefore, we needed to compile the TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 107.74000000000001,
          "end": 109.11,
          "en": "to JavaScript first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 109.11,
          "end": 110.82,
          "en": "to then run the JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 113.81,
          "en": "So that we during development can use TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 113.81,
          "end": 116.47999999999999,
          "en": "but Node still executes JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 116.47999999999999,
          "end": 117.59,
          "en": "So with that up and running,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 117.59,
          "end": 119.46000000000001,
          "en": "we can now send the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 119.46000000000001,
          "end": 122.64,
          "en": "I'm running on localhost 3000,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 122.64,
          "end": 126.41,
          "en": "So therefore, to localhost 3000,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 126.41,
          "end": 128.22,
          "en": "we can send a GET request like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 130.27,
          "en": "And this gives us all the todo's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 130.27,
          "end": 131.87,
          "en": "And you'll see I get back a response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 131.87,
          "end": 134.48,
          "en": "but of course we have no todo's yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 134.48,
          "end": 136.41,
          "en": "So let's send another request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 136.41,
          "end": 139.28,
          "en": "a POST request to create a new todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 139.28,
          "end": 142.183,
          "en": "To localhost 3000/todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 147.34,
          "end": 148.633,
          "en": "This once's a request body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 148.633,
          "end": 152.55,
          "en": "which should be raw and then JSON.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 152.55,
          "end": 153.92000000000002,
          "en": "And in that request body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 153.92000000000002,
          "end": 155.69,
          "en": "if we take a look at that route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 155.69,
          "end": 157.358,
          "en": "we try to extract the text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 157.358,
          "end": 160.82,
          "en": "So we should make sure that this text exists there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 160.82,
          "end": 163.84,
          "en": "So here I'll set a text field in this JSON data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 163.84,
          "end": 165.86,
          "en": "I attached to the outgoing request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 165.86,
          "end": 168.9,
          "en": "And that could be my first todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 168.9,
          "end": 171.24,
          "en": "Make sure you write valid JSON here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 171.24,
          "end": 173.39,
          "en": "with the opening and closing curly brace,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 173.39,
          "end": 175.91,
          "en": "and then your properties between double quotes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 175.91,
          "end": 177.44,
          "en": "and then on the right side of the colon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 177.44,
          "end": 178.97,
          "en": "your values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 178.97,
          "end": 180.04,
          "en": "And if we send this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 180.04,
          "end": 183.373,
          "en": "I get back to 201 response with the todo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 183.373,
          "end": 186.743,
          "en": "that was created and the new todos array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 187.77,
          "end": 190.5,
          "en": "I will now also send a second todo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 190.5,
          "end": 193.83,
          "en": "by just sending the request again with changed data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 193.83,
          "end": 195.89,
          "en": "And if we now send the GET request again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 195.89,
          "end": 198.68,
          "en": "we now see that we got those todos here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 198.68,
          "end": 200.2,
          "en": "Only in memory of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 200.2,
          "end": 203.49,
          "en": "so that data will be lost whenever we shut down this server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 203.49,
          "end": 206.22,
          "en": "But to play around with TypeScript and get those basics,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 206.22,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "that's enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 208.67000000000002,
          "en": "Throughout the course you'll learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 208.67000000000002,
          "end": 211.703,
          "en": "how you can work with files and databases and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 213.34,
          "end": 215.37,
          "en": "So let's now try the other requests as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 215.37,
          "end": 220.37,
          "en": "Let's set a PUT request to localhost 3000/todo/.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 222.29,
          "end": 224.27,
          "en": "And now we need a todo ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 224.27,
          "end": 228.69,
          "en": "So now we'll just grab this ID here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 228.69,
          "end": 230.233,
          "en": "and add that to the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 231.75,
          "end": 233.38,
          "en": "And then add a body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 233.38,
          "end": 235.823,
          "en": "which should be of type JSON of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 236.84,
          "end": 238.793,
          "en": "where I add a new text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 240.41,
          "end": 241.243,
          "en": "So here I'll say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 241.243,
          "end": 245.77,
          "en": "updated todo as a text and send this, it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 245.77,
          "end": 247.76,
          "en": "And if we now fetch all todos again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 247.76,
          "end": 250.653,
          "en": "we of course see the updated todo here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 252.89,
          "end": 257.78,
          "en": "Now we can simply copy that URL and send a last request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 257.78,
          "end": 261.08,
          "en": "a DELETE request here to that same URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 261.08,
          "end": 264.95,
          "en": "So localhost 3000/todo, and then the ID of the todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 264.95,
          "end": 267.77,
          "en": "No data attached, just a DELETE request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 267.77,
          "end": 270.87,
          "en": "If I send it, I get back my success response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 270.87,
          "end": 272.62,
          "en": "And of course, if we get all todos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 272.62,
          "end": 274.58,
          "en": "we see that it was deleted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 274.58,
          "end": 276.1,
          "en": "So the API works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 276.1,
          "end": 279.54,
          "en": "And that's now an API built with TypeScript and Node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 279.54,
          "end": 282.18,
          "en": "Now, I'm not entirely done with it yet though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 282.18,
          "end": 284.719,
          "en": "Let me quit the server with Ctrl + C.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 284.719,
          "end": 286.62,
          "en": "And let's dig a bit deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 286.62,
          "end": 289.01,
          "en": "into this TypeScript Node project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 289.01,
          "end": 290.36,
          "en": "and what we can do with it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
